+### 1549 — App Sandbox restores PlugInKit discovery and physical Gate P0 passes (TASK-260715-9yp8to)
+- ROOT CAUSE: `neagent` previously received zero PlugInKit matches because both the development-signed host and embedded packet-tunnel provider omitted `com.apple.security.app-sandbox`. Adding App Sandbox to both exact targets made PlugInKit discover one provider at the expected embedded path after launch; Network Extension stayed exactly `packet-tunnel-provider`, with no App Groups or signed Keychain Sharing entitlement.
+- PHYSICAL RESULT: On the designated arm64 Mac15,9 running macOS 26.5/Xcode 26.5, the rebuilt archive passed 49 inside-out inspection assertions and nine negative drift cases. Ten start/message/stop cycles plus host termination exited 0 with one manager and no provider process; exact-path user-Applications uninstall/reinstall, PlugInKit rediscovery, and a final cycle also exited 0. No probe crash report or privacy finding was present.
+- ANOMALY/FIX: The first successful ten-cycle lifecycle attempt ended with runner exit 1 because `scutil --nc list` identifies the manager as `[VPN:works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac]`, not by the provider identifier. The manager-count parser now uses that exact host configuration ID and has a provider-decoy regression test; the clean rerun exits 0. Four contract tests pass with 91.80% coverage for `ProbeContract.swift`.
+- UNRELATED REGRESSION CHECK: An extra full `swift test` run built but exited 1 with 377/378 passing when `HEVUDPDatagramAdapterTests/nonterminalRelayErrorsPreserveAssociation` transiently observed zero active associations; the exact test immediately passed alone. A full retry later stopped emitting output and was cancelled after roughly two minutes (exit 130, one cancellation handler pending). This code is outside the probe rework and no aggregate-suite pass is claimed; all task-scoped gates exit 0.
+
 ### 0454 — Physical Gate P0 reaches the macOS VPN approval boundary (TASK-260715-9yp8to)
 - PASS: On the designated arm64 Mac15,9 running macOS 26.5/Xcode 26.5, the accepted archive passed all 47 nested signature, designated-requirement, profile, entitlement, architecture, and privacy assertions. Four contract tests pass with 91.80% line coverage for `ProbeContract.swift`; the new physical-runner parser/privacy tests and lint gates pass.
